WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:13.330
Here at the Akvarel orphanage, the day begins
at seven a.m.

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:20.769
Everyone knows what to do.

00:00:20.769 --> 00:00:30.779
They take the same medications in the same
dosage, mornings and evenings.

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:35.840
Akvarel is home to forty boys and girls from
four to seventeen years old.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:41.140
They're called 'plusiki' and 'minusiki', the
terms for HIV-positive and negative children

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.820
here.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:51.730
"When we opened this home twelve years ago,
at first, the HIV-positive children were kept

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:52.730
separate.

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:58.020
The sofas could be wiped clean, the floors
had no rugs.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.040
The dishes were soaked in disinfectant in
big containers.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.490
It was very hard to create a tolerant environment
for them.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:13.710
It took six years before all the staff members
learned to accept and respect these children."

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.620
Now, the 'plusiki' and 'minusiki' play together.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:20.450
They all have much the same routine.

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:25.200
They're all growing up without parents in
this one-of-a-kind home in the southern Russian

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.670
city of Chelyabinsk.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:33.240
Now, everyone here knows there's no danger
of picking up the virus from the HIV-positive

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:37.790
children - not even if someone should suffer
a cut.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:42.850
Caregivers are never far from the youngest
kids, and the older ones know the virus is

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:49.320
instable and dies if it comes in contact with
air.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:56.360
"One of my friends sleeps in the same room
with me.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.619
He's HIV-positive.

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:03.330
One day before I found out, I came in, and
he said, I've got to tell you something: I'm

00:02:03.330 --> 00:02:04.330
HIV-positive.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:10.179
I was scared at first, but then he told me
how it's transmitted.

00:02:10.179 --> 00:02:12.379
And since then, everything's been OK.

00:02:12.379 --> 00:02:16.310
I treat him completely normally."

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:21.349
One third of the children here were born of
HIV-positive parents - many of whom were also

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:23.980
alcohol or drug-abusers.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:26.620
They lost custody of the children.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:33.430
Some of the parents don't even know where
their children are.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.670
At Akvarel, they grow up in a safe environment.

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:41.470
They learn from the start to approach their
HIV infection with confidence - unlike many

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:44.029
adults.

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:49.140
"Once, our kids went to a summer camp.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.040
The first evening, the children were bathed.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:57.420
The door opened, and the camp director peeked
in - as if our children had four ears and

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.900
two heads!

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:01.809
Another time, my co-worker asked, 'Marina,
what should I do?

00:03:01.809 --> 00:03:04.209
They've brought us an H-I-V-positive boy'.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:06.090
I said, 'Off to the cellar with him.

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:07.220
Lock him up!

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.220
She was bewildered.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.959
I said, 'What do you think?

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:14.239
Let him play with the others, of course!"

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:19.900
As the day closes at Akvarel, everyone knows
just what to do: the same medications in the

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.180
same dosages - every evening.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.889
Everyone here is worried about what will become
of the kids once they leave the home.

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:34.309
Many of them were born with disabilities because
of their mothers' alcohol or drug abuse.

00:03:34.309 --> 00:03:39.150
Unless they are adopted, they will likely
be left to fend for themselves for the rest

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:55.319
of their lives.

